# We get filled long, then the market falls until the loss limit ($100)
# trips at a timer tick.
#
# Sellers hit our bid repeatedly while the market steps down a few cents at
# a time. The loss is only checked on the timer, marked to the mid sampled
# there. Once it breaches, the app cancels everything and stops quoting.
#
# Participants: 2 and 3 provide the book, 4 takes liquidity.

latency market_data 5_000
latency order_entry 10_000
timer 1_000_000
end 40_000_000

0            2 enter 1 B 500 100.00
0            3 enter 1 S 500 100.01

# Each round: sell through our bid, then the whole market re-forms 5 cents
# lower (bids first, then asks, then the old asks are pulled).
2_000_000    4 enter 1 S 600 99.99 ioc
3_000_000    2 enter 2 B 500 99.95
3_000_000    3 enter 2 S 500 99.96
3_000_100    3 cancel 1

5_000_000    4 enter 2 S 600 99.94 ioc
6_000_000    2 enter 3 B 500 99.90
6_000_000    3 enter 3 S 500 99.91
6_000_100    3 cancel 2

8_000_000    4 enter 3 S 600 99.89 ioc
9_000_000    2 enter 4 B 500 99.85
9_000_000    3 enter 4 S 500 99.86
9_000_100    3 cancel 3

11_000_000   4 enter 4 S 600 99.84 ioc
12_000_000   2 enter 5 B 500 99.80
12_000_000   3 enter 5 S 500 99.81
12_000_100   3 cancel 4

# No more fills; the market keeps falling. Each step pulls the old bid
# first, so the new ask doesn't trade against it.
15_000_000   2 cancel 5
15_000_000   2 enter 6 B 500 99.70
15_000_100   3 enter 6 S 500 99.71
15_000_100   3 cancel 5

18_000_000   2 cancel 6
18_000_000   2 enter 7 B 500 99.60
18_000_100   3 enter 7 S 500 99.61
18_000_100   3 cancel 6

21_000_000   2 cancel 7
21_000_000   2 enter 8 B 500 99.50
21_000_100   3 enter 8 S 500 99.51
21_000_100   3 cancel 7
